{"item":{"body":{"text":"Check divisibility up to sqrt(391) ≈ 19.77. Primes: 2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19.\n\n391 is odd, not div by 2. 3+9+1=13, not div by 3. Not by 5. 7: 7×55=385, remainder 6. 11: 11×35=385, remainder 6. 13: 13×30=390, remainder 1. 17: 17×23=391! 17×23 = 391. Yes: 17×23 = 340 + 51 = 391. So 391 is composite.","type":"reasoning"},"id":"msg_0eb7320a9001vve3OV5uNi2HRT:reasoning:0","parent":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"item":{"body":{"text":"√391 ≈ 19.8, so I need to test primes 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19: it's odd, digits sum to 13, doesn't end in 0/5, and 7×55=385, 11×35=385, 13×30=390 leave remainders — but 17×23 = 391 exactly, so the search stops there.\n\n391 is not prime: it's the product 17 × 23.","type":"message"},"id":"msg_0eb7320a9001vve3OV5uNi2HRT:text:0","parent":null,"status":"completed"}}
